WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.478
Which cloud matters at every step:
the sign-in authority, the Graph host,

2
00:00:04.478 --> 00:00:07.609
the Azure environment,
the token audience and the

3
00:00:07.609 --> 00:00:10.663
Graph PowerShell environment
all have to agree.

4
00:00:10.663 --> 00:00:13.043
For a GCC tenant like this estate's,

5
00:00:13.043 --> 00:00:16.699
Learn says apps keep using
the worldwide endpoints.

6
00:00:16.699 --> 00:00:21.176
The higher clouds share a government
sign-in authority, and here's the trap:

7
00:00:21.176 --> 00:00:24.405
the Azure sign-in environment
is the same for GCC High

8
00:00:24.405 --> 00:00:27.487
and the Defense cloud, but
their Graph hosts differ.

9
00:00:27.487 --> 00:00:31.813
So the Graph host must come from the
cloud profile, never from the sign-in.

10
00:00:31.813 --> 00:00:34.820
An unknown cloud name is refused outright.
